  "text": "The map itself is a machine. [short pause] Nothing you're seeing is hand-placed: a layout engine solves the whole estate — districts on rings around the manor, a road reserved from the gate, every label guaranteed room to breathe.\n\n[pause] It even has a conscience: a self-test that fails the build if the map ever gets too crowded to read. A map with a legibility guarantee. [short pause] This month the estate reorganized itself — the collection had sprawled flat, so it was regathered into districts, with buildings that advertise their depth. [pause] I mention it because it is the truest thing about this place: it is not a portfolio. It is a town, and a town has to keep working as it grows.",
